<title>BRAZIL: Banco CCF Brasil prices $100 mln bonds.</title>
<headline>Banco CCF Brasil prices $100 mln bonds.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco CCF Brasil, a unit of Credit Commercial de France, said it launched $100 million in three-year bonds Wednesday.</p>
<p>The bonds will pay a coupon of 7.75 percent semi-annually and were priced at 100.48, offering a spread of 165 basis points over three-year U.S. Treasury notes, the bank said in a statement. The deal matures on July 28, 2000.</p>
<p>The issue is the second drawdown on a $400 million medium-term note program begun in June 1996, the statement said.</p>
<p>((--John Miller, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248-5414)</p>
